\begin{center}\vspace*{2cm}{\Large\bfseries Supplement T}\par\vspace{1cm}
{\large General Theta Foundations I:\\Acquired Geometry and Causal Resource Transfer}\par\vspace{1cm}
Qian Qi\par\vspace{0.5cm}8 October 2026\end{center}\vspace{1.5cm}
This is an integral submitted supplement, not a separate publication. It supplies in full the autonomous separated-refinement, continuation-geometry, acquired-rank, filtering and causal-resource proofs retained from the preceding manuscript. Its definitions and assumptions remain in force; its independent theorem numbering refers to this supplement.

The attached complete mathematical text has not been abridged. In particular, its separated-refinement completion theorem is horizon-uniform on its stated certificate class, whereas the new posterior-pooling theorem in the accompanying article has an explicit horizon factor. Its noisy continuation theorems are not restated as unrestricted adaptive-control results.

Supplement S, also supplied in full, contains the earlier technical block-stability and instrument arguments cited by this text. The accompanying article contains the new overlapping-noise adaptive-pooling theorem and does not use a realization to prove that theorem.
